WATCHED-CANDIDATE PROJECTION (labeled projection, not observation — for
higher concurrency): queue-claim latency is the expected first degrader
once real seats claim real rows under contention. This run could not
observe it (cold rows by design, zero seat claims); the next exercise
that runs N>3 slices with live claimants MUST measure create→claim per
row and promote this projection to an observed bottleneck or retire it.

